the Minoan After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and 
Bead-Seals from Thisbe, Boeotia\". Childe situates the work within the broader 
recognition that classical Greek civilization was preceded and rooted in the 
Minoan culture of Crete and its Mycenaean counterpart. The review notes Evans’s 
role as excavator of Minos’s palace at Knossos and his contributions in tracing 
Minoan influence on classical Greece. Childe comments on Evans’s interpretation 
of the Ring of Nestor and the associated treasure, highlighting how the study 
illuminates aspects of Minoan funerary beliefs and art and contributes to our 
understanding of pre-classical Greek civilization. The review also provides 
