    "relevance_to_query": "High. Provides contextual information on the Griffin 
Warrior tomb at Pylos and the assemblage of gold signet rings with Minoan ritual
scenes; useful for situating the Ring of Nestor within broader Aegean 
signet-ring scholarship and for non-Wikipedia-style citation practices on 
related material.",
    "retrieved_content_or_summary": "The site, maintained by the Griffin Warrior
project, presents an overview of the discovery and excavation of the Griffin 
Warrior tomb near the Palace of Nestor in Pylos. It explains that the tomb was 
discovered in May 2015 by a University of Cincinnati archaeological team and 
dates to the Late Helladic IIA period. The grave contained the remains of a 
single elite male buried with an unusually rich assemblage of grave goods, 
including weapons, seal stones, jewelry, and multiple gold signet rings 
decorated with Minoan ritual scenes. The text describes the excavation process, 
the context of the tomb within the Bronze Age landscape (including proximity to 
tholos tombs and the Palace of Nestor), and emphasizes the importance of the 
finds for understanding Mycenaean–Minoan interaction and elite identity. 
Although it does not focus specifically on the Ring of Nestor from Thisbê, its 
discussion of the Griffin Warrior’s gold rings and their iconography provides 
comparative material on Aegean gold signet rings and demonstrates standards of 
archaeological reporting, which can inform how to structure and source a 
Wikipedia-style article with inline citations."
