### 4. Theodore Eliopoulos, “SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING 
OF NESTOR’” (2013)

- **Title**: SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’
- **URL**: 
https://www.academia.edu/83658257/SOME_OBSERVATIONS_ON_THE_ICONOGRAPHY_OF_THE_RI
NG_OF_NESTOR_
- **Domain**: academia.edu
- **Source type**: Academic article / conference or journal paper hosted on 
Academia.edu.
- **Date**: 2013 (noted in the page: *2013, ANNUARIO della Scuola Archeologica 
di Atene e delle Missioni Italiane in Oriente*).[4]
- **Triggered by query**: `"Ring of Nestor" signet ring Evans 1925 authenticity 
OJA 17 1-13`
- **Raw / summarized content**:
  - Presents an analysis of the iconography of the Ring of Nestor within the 
larger context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates.[4]
  - Emphasizes contradictions between technical analyses and iconographic 
evidence, arguing that iconography plays an essential role in assessing 
authenticity in Aegean studies.[4]
  - Discusses the relationship between incurved altars depicted on the ring and 
similar motifs elsewhere, suggesting this strengthens the case for 
authenticity.[4]
