      "local_ref": "d1",
      "document_summary": "Heidelberg University Library’s digital page provides
full scanned access to Arthur J. Evans’s 1925 work on the Ring of Nestor and 
associated gold signet rings and bead-seals from a rock-cut sepulchral context 
near Thisbê in Boeotia. It lists the internal structure of the publication: a 
title page; Part I, titled “Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia” (pp. 1–42), which describes the discovery 
context, location, the assemblage of rings and bead-seals, their physical 
features, images, dating and cultural attribution; Part II, titled “A glimpse 
into the Minoan after-world” (pp. 43–75), which interprets the iconography and 
religious or afterlife implications of the Ring of Nestor; and plates I–V 
containing illustrations. The work treats the assemblage as late Mycenaean and 
compares it with other Aegean material.",
      "source_ref": "s1"
