"关于“涅斯托尔指环”真伪的评估存在冲突：有文献基于技术观察支持其为真品（如技术研
究文章），而另有中20世纪研究提出风格和图像异常可能指向伪造。", "conflict_type": 
"factual", "source_ids": ["20260628151426814079_534983c2", 
"20260628151426724745_00803f3e"]}, {"id": "20260628151429315658_a483f97b", 
"description": 
"对“涅斯托尔指环”的发现背景与墓葬宝藏性质的可靠性存在分歧：埃文斯在1925年的专著
和期刊文章中将其视为来自博奥提亚西斯贝的墓葬宝藏，而1948年的批判性研究则质疑其来
源链与墓葬情境的可信度。", "conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426814079_534983c2", "20260628151426747249_a4a92d79"]}, {"id": 
"20260628152158934683_6bf415c1", "description": "Different sources express 
opposing views on the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor: some describe it as a 
likely forgery or ‘pseudo-Minoan’, while others argue strongly for its 
authenticity based on iconographic and technical evidence.", "conflict_type": 
"factual", "source_ids": ["20260628151607771821_88154e17", 
"20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3", "20260628152155774552_30f3d9fd", 
"20260628151426767673_92082ca0"]}, {"id": "20260628152359868437_b1198886", 
"description": "Different sources assign different date ranges for the Ring of 
Nestor, with one study dating it to ca. 1700–1450 BCE and another to the 
16th–15th century BC.", "conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426767673_92082ca0", "20260628152356217660_e3acb55e"]}, {"id": 
"20260628152359941990_81a11d93", "description": "Scholars disagree on the 
authenticity of the Ring of Nestor: some articles characterize it as 
pseudo‑Minoan and emphasize that many condemned it as a forgery, while others 
argue that new comparative material supports its authenticity.", 
"conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": ["20260628152356361925_b462029c", 
"20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3", "20260628151426767673_92082ca0", 
"20260628152155774552_30f3d9fd"]}, {"id": "20260628152400055548_46570885", 
"description": "Interpretations of a key guardian figure on the Ring of Nestor’s
scene differ, with Arthur Evans describing it as a watch‑dog or dragon guarding 
the tree of the world and Vlachopoulos reinterpreting it as a scorpion attacking
a dragon‑like creature.", "conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426747249_a4a92d79", "20260628151426767673_92082ca0"]}, {"id": 
"20260628152407827414_3ad0d710", "description": "Potential differences in 
emphasis on the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor: Arthur Evans’s 1925 
monograph and subsequent positive reception (e.g., Childe’s review) treat the 
ring as an authentic artifact illuminating Minoan beliefs, while Theodore 
Eliopoulos’s 2013 article situates the ring within debates on Aegean forgeries 
and notes contradictions in technical analyses, even as it presents iconographic
arguments supporting authenticity.", "conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3", "20260628151426699067_72f930f4", 
"20260628152221170593_22faa1dc"]}, {"id": "20260628152407939872_bada46e9", 
"description": "Minor variation in description of the Ring of Nestor’s physical 
specifications: the JSTOR snippet explicitly mentions a weight of 31.5 grams and
a funereal pendant type hoop, while the Heidelberg digitized monograph also 
provides measurements and construction details that may or may not exactly match
the summarized weight and typological description from the JSTOR entry.", 
"conflict_type": "factual", "source_ids": ["20260628152221170593_22faa1dc", 
