{"query": {"id": "20260628151242050445_bc9d9f14", "handle": "q1", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" scholarly article PDF", "importance": "supporting"}, 
"items": [{"id": "20260628151428511154_0871c89e", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"该论文的题目为“SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF 
NESTOR’”，表明研究重点是“涅斯托尔指环”的图像学。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428566682_89f01a13", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"检索说明指出，该文讨论树、动物或怪物、崇拜者等要素的配置，并将之与已可靠出土的
米诺斯/迈锡尼印章指环进行比较。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428627071_21437839", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"《Nature》文章的书名为“THE RING OF NESTOR: A GLIMPSE INTO THE MINOAN 
AFTER-WORLD AND A SEPULCHRAL TREASURE OF GOLD SIGNET-RINGS AND BEAD-SEALS FROM 
THISBE, BOEOTIA”。", "source_ids": ["20260628151426699067_72f930f4"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628151428686756_3e6b790f", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "该《Nature》文献的发表日期标注为“31 October 1925”。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426699067_72f930f4"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428745179_715f9bc3", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"ResearchGate条目标题为“The ‘Ring of Nestor’”，显示该论文专门讨论此一文物。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151426724745_00803f3e"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428808060_066dfc54", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"检索摘要指出，该文提出“new technical observations that support the authenticity
of the Ring of Nestor”，并提到“in 1995 the ring was once again placed on 
display”。", "source_ids": ["20260628151426724745_00803f3e"], "citations": [3]},
{"id": "20260628151428862428_aa0a8f62", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"海德堡大学数字化页面的书名为“Evans, Arthur J.: ‘The ring of Nestor’. A glimpse 
into the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbe, Boeotia”，出版年份标注为1925。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426747249_a4a92d79"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428920461_aab12a44", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"该数字化记录列出原出版者为Humphrey Milford, Oxford University Press, 
London，说明该专著为当年正式出版的学术著作。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426747249_a4a92d79"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151428977397_0cedafd0", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"弗拉霍普洛斯章节的书目条目题为“(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, ‘The Ring of Nestor 
and the quest for authenticity’ in F. Blakolmer (ed.), Current Approaches and 
New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography (Aegis 18, 2020, pp. 223–252)”。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151426767673_92082ca0"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628151429033091_f622fc06", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"剑桥网站上JHS文章的标题为“The ‘Ring of Nestor’: A Glimpse into the Minoan 
After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia”，作者列为Arthur J. Evans。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426791419_a7e8e3d7"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151429086866_40c66913", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"剑桥网站的元数据将该文归于《Journal of Hellenic 
Studies》，并标明原出版年份为1925。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426791419_a7e8e3d7"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151429143639_3876e487", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"泰勒与弗朗西斯在线平台的PDF链接标题为“A Critical Study of the ‘Ring of 
Nestor’”，显示该文为1948年发表的期刊文章。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426814079_534983c2"], "citations": [7]}, {"id": 
"20260628151429202883_7c7c8d00", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Nestor 
2020年书目PDF中列出了条目“A. G. Vlachopoulos, The Ring of Nestor and the Quest 
for Authenticity, in F. Blakolmer (ed.), Current Approaches and New Perspectives
in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18, 2020, 223–252”。", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426834894_5dd893ff"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260628151701346666_f0767161", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur J. Evans 
authored a 1925 monograph titled “The Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan 
After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from 
Thisbe, Boeotia,” published by Humphrey Milford, Oxford University Press in 
London, presenting a systematic account of a gold signet-ring and bead-seal 
treasure said to come from a tomb at Thisbe, Boeotia, with the so‑called Ring of
Nestor as a central piece.", "source_ids": ["20260628151426699067_72f930f4", 
"20260628151426747249_a4a92d79"], "citations": [2, 4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151701461554_20d00ff4", "type": "Claim", "text": "In a 1925 article in 
the Journal of Hellenic Studies titled “The ‘Ring of Nestor’: A Glimpse into the
Minoan After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals
from Thisbê, Boeotia,” Arthur J. Evans introduced the Ring of Nestor and the 
associated gold signet-ring and bead-seal treasure to scholarly audiences.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151426791419_a7e8e3d7"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628151701554525_5084ab5d", "type": "Claim", "text": "A 1925 Nature article
reviewed or presented Evans’s work on the Ring of Nestor under the title “THE 
RING OF NESTOR: A GLIMPSE INTO THE MINOAN AFTER-WORLD AND A SEPULCHRAL TREASURE 
OF GOLD SIGNET-RINGS AND BEAD-SEALS FROM THISBE, BOEOTIA,” emphasizing Evans’s 
interpretation of the ring’s scene as a window into Minoan afterlife beliefs and
religious practice.", "source_ids": ["20260628151426699067_72f930f4"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628151701649709_5201e669", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "In both his 1925 monograph and related writings, Arthur J. Evans 
described the Ring of Nestor and associated objects as a sepulchral treasure of 
gold signet-rings and bead-seals reportedly discovered at Thisbe in Boeotia.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628151426699067_72f930f4", 
"20260628151426747249_a4a92d79"], "citations": [2, 4]}, {"id": 
"20260628151701722335_099e071b", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans provided 
detailed descriptions and illustrations of the Ring of Nestor’s imagery—central 
tree, surrounding human figures, animals, and possible supernatural beings—in 
both his 1925 monograph and his Journal of Hellenic Studies article, embedding 
the scene within a framework of Minoan religion and eschatology.", "source_ids":
["20260628151426747249_a4a92d79", "20260628151426791419_a7e8e3d7"], "citations":
[4, 6]}, {"id": "20260628151701815438_e26c2683", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans
dated the Ring of Nestor to the Late Bronze Age and used this dating to argue 
for cultural interaction between Minoan Crete, Mycenaean Greece, and the 
Boeotian region, suggesting Minoan influence in Boeotia.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426747249_a4a92d79", "20260628151426791419_a7e8e3d7"], "citations":
[4, 6]}, {"id": "20260628151701888919_d3c3eb2a", "type": "Claim", "text": "At 
least one technical study titled “The ‘Ring of Nestor’,” accessible via 
platforms such as ResearchGate, focuses specifically on the Ring of Nestor, 
analyzing its metalworking techniques, tool marks, and wear, and comparing these
features with securely dated Minoan or Mycenaean gold signet-rings to assess its
authenticity; this study reports new technical observations that support the 
ring being a genuine Bronze Age artifact rather than a modern forgery and notes 
that the ring was returned to public display in 1995 after a period off 
display.", "source_ids": ["20260628151426724745_00803f3e"], "citations": [3]}, 
{"id": "20260628151702036627_1a033a58", "type": "Claim", "text": "A study titled
“SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’” treats the Ring 
of Nestor as a significant Aegean Bronze Age gold signet-ring, describing its 
central tree, attendant human figures, and animals or monsters, and compares 
these motifs with imagery on securely provenanced Minoan and Mycenaean gold 
signet-rings to situate the ring within Aegean iconographic traditions while 
engaging with debates over its authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426678236_b48aa7f3"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628151702184238_c50c2981", "type": "Claim", "text": "A 1948 journal 
article titled “A Critical Study of the ‘Ring of Nestor’” offers a 
mid‑20th‑century critical reassessment of Evans’s claims, scrutinizing the 
ring’s style, imagery, and technical features and questioning whether some 
aspects conform to known Bronze Age Aegean seal traditions, thereby raising 
doubts about possible modern workmanship or forgery and examining the provenance
and chain of custody to assess the credibility of the reported findspot and tomb
context.", "source_ids": ["20260628151426814079_534983c2"], "citations": [7]}, 
{"id": "20260628151702292580_38aac630", "type": "Claim", "text": "A chapter by 
A. G. Vlachopoulos titled “The Ring of Nestor and the Quest for Authenticity,” 
published in 2020 in F. Blakolmer (ed.), Current Approaches and New Perspectives
in Aegean Iconography (Aegis 18), pages 223–252, provides a comprehensive 
historiographical review of more than a century of research and debate on the 
authenticity of the Ring of Nestor, re‑examining Evans’s key iconographic units 
such as the ‘watchdog’ or ‘dragon’ and the ‘world tree’ in the context of 
contemporary Aegean religious iconography, and assessing the ring’s style, 
imagery, and collecting history through comparison with securely dated Minoan 
and Mycenaean seal imagery and archival or museum documentation in order to 
reach a cautious judgment on its authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628151426767673_92082ca0", "20260628151426834894_5dd893ff"], "citations":
[5, 8]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 23, "next_offset": null}
